    "narrative": "With the season nearing its conclusion, the Austin Waves lineup remains focused on maximizing efficiency against today\u2019s slate, anchored by **Sam Antonacci** (58.38). **Sam Antonacci** represents our strongest play, bolstered by a favorable matchup against Blubaugh and a +7% boost from a platoon advantage; batting lead-off provides the necessary volume to capitalize on his current form. **Jackson Merrill** (54.13) also commands a start despite facing a southpaw in Boyd, as his ability to contribute across all five categories\u2014including his secondary value in the stolen base market\u2014outweighs the marginal hit he takes from the platoon dynamic. \n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved balancing the production of **Miguel Vargas** (50.48) against the overall roster construction; while **Miguel Vargas** maintains a solid score, his utility is somewhat capped today by the matchup against Blubaugh. We are navigating significant lineup uncertainty with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (41.87) and **Heliot Ramos** (46.77), both of whom are projected based on assumed lineup slots. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** faces a tough assignment against Tolle, and his efficiency score sits right on the border of our \"Marginal\" threshold; he remains in the starting nine primarily for his potential to chip into our SB scarcity. **Drake Baldwin** (47.58) is similarly positioned as a high-volume play, though we are monitoring his matchup against Luzardo closely, as the SP\u2019s skill set suppresses the ceiling of our catchers today.\n\nWe are entering the day with several key assets sidelined, including **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who are all unavailable due to scheduled off-days. Furthermore, **Luis Robert Jr.** remains on the IL, limiting our depth as we chase production in these final categories. We advise monitoring the final confirmed lineups for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Heliot Ramos**, as any shift downward in their batting order will necessitate an immediate re-evaluation of their projected utility and our risk exposure to the opposing pitching staff.",
